	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper states that the Donor Heart Study was a “5-year multicenter observational prospective cohort study.” The machine-learning method was unsupervised “k-means clustering,” using all 17 segment-level wall motion scores from transthoracic echocardiography to identify RWMA phenotypes. The number of clusters was chosen using the cubic clustering criterion, but no held-out validation, SHAP/LIME-style interpretability method, or hyperparameter-tuning procedure was reported.  ￼

