	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: The analysis excluded donors without adequate initial TTE quality and then excluded 70 outliers after cluster analysis, which is most consistent with complete case analysis plus exclusions rather than imputation. Class imbalance handling was not relevant because this was unsupervised phenotyping rather than a binary classifier. Data preprocessing was described: only donors with RWMA on initial TTE entered clustering, 17 segment-specific WMS values were used, 8 preliminary clusters were generated and then consolidated into 4 clinically plausible phenotypes, and 70 outliers were excluded. Code availability was not reported.  ￼

