	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: This was not a supervised prediction model with held-out discrimination metrics. Instead, the clinically relevant outcomes associated with the RWMA phenotypes were donor-heart acceptance, changes in LVEF/WMSI on follow-up TTE, and recipient survival after transplantation. Table 1 reports donor-heart acceptance was highest in FBS (68.2%), and recipient 2-year survival among transplanted hearts was similar across phenotypes. Figure 3 shows all phenotypes improved in LVEF on second echocardiogram. Because no AUC, accuracy, PPV, sensitivity, specificity, NPV, F1-score, calibration, or DCA were reported for a predictive model, those fields are NR/No.

